messages.content:
REQUIRED JSON SHAPE (use exactly these keys — the host parser rejects alternate shapes):
  {"tool_call": "<registry_name>", "args": { ... }}

WRONG (do not emit): "name", "tool", "parameters", "strategy_id", OpenAI "function" wrappers, or mixing Lorenz parameters with graph_reduce fields.

When you have gathered enough evidence (include curated_context for the downstream reasoning agent):
  {"final_answer": {"curated_context": {"confidence": 0.0, "what_this_context_is": "...", "primary_event_ids": []},
   "response": "...", "suggested_nodes": [{"event_id": "...", "confidence": 0.0, "rationale": "..."}], "gaps": ["..."]}}

Parameter rules:
- Time windows: ONLY in graph_reduce args: recent_years, temporal_anchor, temporal_start, temporal_end (plus drop_* flags).
- graph_pe_lorenz_classify args: event_ids, rho, tau, steps — NEVER put temporal_* or recent_years here.
- graph_bfs_expand: use "edge_types": ["temporal"] (list of strings). NOT "connascence_type".

Examples:
{"tool_call":"graph_reduce","args":{"drop_page":true,"drop_unknown_timestamp":false,"drop_isolates":true,"recent_years":5.0,"temporal_anchor":"latest_in_corpus"}}
{"tool_call":"graph_bfs_expand","args":{"seed_event_ids":["pdf_x_e0001"],"max_depth":3,"restrict_to_event_ids":["..."],"edge_types":["temporal"]}}
{"tool_call":"graph_pe_lorenz_classify","args":{"event_ids":["..."],"rho":28.0,"tau":2.0,"steps":1500}}

RULES:
- One JSON object per turn — tool_call+args OR final_answer. No markdown fences, no prose.
- event_ids must come from tool output or seeds.
- Up to 6 tool turns; then final_answer.

Available tools:

  graph_snapshot (S1): PTV shape: types, date ranges, per-node edge counts.
    default args: {}
  graph_reduce (S2): Drop page / unknown-date / isolate nodes (configurable).
    default args: {"drop_page": true, "drop_unknown_timestamp": true, "drop_isolates": true}
  graph_token_budget (S3): Rank events and pack into max_tokens budget.
    default args: {"event_ids": [], "max_tokens": 12000, "query": "", "prefer_recent": true}
  graph_bfs_expand (S4): BFS from one seed or many (seed_event_ids); optional restrict_to_event_ids keeps expansion on a subgraph (e.g. post-reduce).
    default args: {"seed_event_id": "", "seed_event_ids": null, "max_depth": 2, "edge_types": null, "max_nodes": 400, "restrict_to_event_ids": null}
  graph_centrality (S5): Degree + sampled betweenness + eigenvector (undirected projection).
    default args: {"event_ids": null, "top_k": 40}
  graph_kcore (S6): k-core decomposition for dense clinical core.
    default args: {"event_ids": null, "k": 2, "max_nodes": 200}
  graph_bridges (S7): Bridges and articulation points (narrative pivots).
    default args: {"event_ids": null, "max_bridges": 80}
  graph_pe_lorenz_classify (S8): Lorenz RK4 wing classification: KEEP / EVICT / REVIEW.
    default args: {"event_ids": [], "rho": 28.0, "tau": 2.0, "steps": 2000}
  graph_pe_sweep (S9): ρ×τ grid on a sample; returns eviction/keep rates.
    default args: {"sample_nodes": 300, "rho_values": null, "tau_values": null}
  graph_pe_govern_adjust (S10): Promote EVICT→REVIEW for load-bearing / dense diagnosis nodes.
    default args: {"items": []}
  graph_hybrid_search (S11): BM25-style keywords + optional sentence-transformers cosine, RRF-fused. Pass event_ids to search only a subset (e.g. after graph_reduce).
    default args: {"query": "", "top_k": 30, "semantic": true, "event_ids": null}
  graph_biomarker_icm (S12): Regex lab series (A1c/CRP/ESR) + lightweight ICM headroom trace.
    default args: {"biomarkers": ["a1c", "crp", "esr"], "ic_max": 100.0}

IMPORTANT: graph_reduce has already been run. You receive `reduced_event_ids` as your starting corpus.
Use these ids in event_ids / restrict_to_event_ids args to stay on the cleaned subgraph.
For temporal slicing, call graph_reduce again with recent_years / temporal_anchor on top of the reduced set.

